%% skill-crud
%% Summary: Run one catalog create, read, update, delete or rename through preflight stops, canonical edits, regeneration, verification, an all-provider build and tests.
%% Sources: skills/skill-crud/core.md
%% Not shown: the request fields, each stop code's trigger, reference dispositions, the per-operation edits, and the report's fields
%% Alt: A request is normalized and preflighted read-only; a failed preflight stops unwritten; a mutation is edited, regenerated, verified, built and tested, and the caller commits.

flowchart TD
    A[Normalize the request] --> B[Preflight: source, prerequisites, inspect]
    B --> C{Preflight passes?}
    C -- No --> D[Stop with its code; nothing written]
    C -- READ --> E[Report and verify; change nothing]
    C -- Yes, a mutation --> F[Record base ref and target hashes]
    F --> G[Edit canonical authoring surfaces only]
    G --> H[Regenerate the three artifacts]
    H --> I[Verify the request read-only]
    I --> J[Build every provider, disposable dir]
    J --> K[Run focused tests and the change pack]
    K --> L{All later gates passed?}
    L -- No --> M[Stop: CATALOG_MUTATION_INCOMPLETE, no cleanup]
    L -- Yes --> N[Report; the caller commits]
